LATENT DISPATCH
Tue Sep 22 · 4 items · ~3 min

PELAGIC 3: WHAT WE KNOW
Three sources say October. Rumored: native multi-document input, a cheaper reasoning mode, and a 4M context nobody asked for. Pricing unknown. If you are planning a Q4 migration, wait for the rate card.

A RETRY BUDGET, NOT A RETRY COUNT
A short, useful design note: instead of "retry 3 times," give each job a token budget and let it retry until the budget is gone. It bounds cost per job rather than per call, and it makes the runaway-job class of incident structurally impossible. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/retry-budget

FERRITE-70B FINE-TUNING RECIPES
Three teams published their recipes for narrow-task fine-tunes: 5k examples, LoRA, one 80GB card, under $200 in compute. The consistent result is a model that beats the base 70B on the target task and costs the same to serve. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/ferrite-recipes

